### 1. Valid signup (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test Owner",
  "email": "owner@example.com",
  "password": "CorrectHorse2026",
  "organizationName": "Test Estates"
}

### 2. Same email again (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test Owner",
  "email": "owner@example.com",
  "password": "CorrectHorse2026",
  "organizationName": "Test Estates"
}

### 3. Weak password and bad email (expect 422 with a details list)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "A",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short",
  "organizationName": "X"
}

### 4. Mass-assignment attempt (expect 422)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Sneaky User",
  "email": "sneaky@example.com",
  "password": "CorrectHorse2026",
  "organizationName": "Sneaky Estates",
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "isSystemAdmin": true
}

### 5. Broken JSON (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName":"Oops",


### 6. Login (expect 200, a Set-Cookie header, and an accessToken in the body)
# @name login
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@example.com", "password": "CorrectHorse2026" }

### 7. Wrong password (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@example.com", "password": "WrongPassword123" }

### 8. Unknown email (expect the IDENTICAL 401 message)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "WrongPassword123" }

### 9. Refresh (expect 200 and a new accessToken; REST Client sends the cookie for you)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/refresh

### 10. Logout (expect 204)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/logout

### 11. Refresh after logout (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/refresh